  "implementation": [
    "DO linkVisitor delegates to a serialized source transition; the session-host path retains its existing behavior.",
    "Source freezes committed profile and immutable transfer identity before target dispatch; durable pending/complete state fences HTTP/WS/buffered/manual/internal import/absorb/forward and alarm behavior.",
    "Target commits profile, receipt and bounded authoritative compatibility members together, then publishes the latest member set and visitor projection under target serialization. KV never selects whether to remerge.",
    "Consent is excluded from immutable identity; current source/target restrictions intersect before first merge, suppress incoming behavior/enrichment under refusal, and later refusals tighten without remerge.",
    "Completed-source retries require the existing target receipt, so a sequential target reset does not recreate the erased profile. In-flight/prepared cross-object erasure remains excluded.",
    "R1: refused first transfer into an existing valid target preserves affinity/pipeline, audienceOwner and timer exactly; no target config resolution, merge/tick/requalification, enrichment merge or timer refresh. Receipt/current members/tightened consent still commit atomically. Cold-target establishment unchanged."
  ],
